\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Project Notocal Pro: Architecture & Blueprint\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 NOtes, TO-dos, CALendars, and PROjects. Not a Pro subscription!\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 1. Core Philosophy & Constraints\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Environment:
\f1\b0  Self-hosted on a home lab, accessed securely via Tailscale.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Data Source of Truth:
\f1\b0  Radicale (CalDAV/CardDAV). Chosen specifically because it stores data as plain 
\f2\fs26 .ics
\f1\fs24  text files, allowing easy read/write access for local AI scripts outside the web app context.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Target Platform:
\f1\b0  Desktop-first web application (Windows), built with modular components to facilitate a future React Native (Android) port.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 UX Paradigm:
\f1\b0  Multi-pane, keyboard-shortcut heavy, modular, and local-first feel.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 2. Tech Stack Definition\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Framework:
\f1\b0  Vite (React SPA) - Highly optimized for heavily stateful, local-first client applications. Avoids the SSR overhead and hydration mismatches of Next.js. Authentication and proxying to Radicale can be handled via direct CORS configuration or a minimal local Node/Express proxy.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Styling:
\f1\b0  Tailwind CSS - Utility-first styling, ensuring an easy migration path to React Native via NativeWind later.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 UI Components:
\f1\b0  
\f2\fs26 shadcn/ui
\f1\fs24  (Radix UI primitives) - Accessible, unstyled components that we own and style with Tailwind.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 State Management & Caching:
\f1\b0  * Zustand - Lightweight global state for UI handling, in-memory drafts, and the relationship graph. Uses 
\f2\fs26 persist
\f1\fs24  middleware.\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl1\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 IndexedDB - Local browser caching to store the CalDAV graph, preventing the need to re-download the entire Radicale flat-file database on every load.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 CalDAV Client:
\f1\b0  
\f2\fs26 tsdav
\f1\fs24  - TypeScript-first library for fetching, parsing, updating, and handling WebDAV sync/ETags.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Icons:
\f1\b0  
\f2\fs26 lucide-react
\f1\fs24  - Clean, consistent iconography.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 3. Data Mapping (CalDAV Standards)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 To maintain compatibility with standard 
\f2\fs26 .ics
\f1\fs24  clients, we strictly adhere to standard properties and use smart parsing for advanced features.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 A. Calendars & Projects (The Cross-Cutting Graph)\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Calendars (The Containers):
\f1\b0  Standard CalDAV calendars (e.g., Work, Personal, Travel). These act as the fundamental toggles and "Areas of Responsibility".\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Projects (The Entities):
\f1\b0  A Project is stored as a 
\f2\fs26 VJOURNAL
\f1\fs24  entity. It can optionally have 
\f2\fs26 DTSTART
\f1\fs24 /
\f2\fs26 DTEND
\f1\fs24  dates. Stored in a dedicated, hidden-by-default Radicale collection (e.g., 
\f2\fs26 /user/system-projects/
\f1\fs24 ).\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl1
\f3\i \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 First Launch Bootstrapping:
\f1\i0  On initial login, the app automatically sends a WebDAV 
\f2\fs26 MKCOL
\f1\fs24 /
\f2\fs26 MKCALENDAR
\f1\fs24  request to ensure 
\f2\fs26 /user/system-projects/
\f1\fs24  exists, preventing 404 errors on fresh Radicale environments.\
\ls3\ilvl1
\f3\i \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Empty Project Handling:
\f1\i0  When created, a Project is explicitly assigned a "Primary Context" (e.g., Work) to ensure it appropriately responds to global calendar filters even before child items are added to it.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Custom Properties:
\f1\b0  * 
\f2\fs26 X-PROJECT-STATUS
\f1\fs24 : Tracks the overall state (Active, Scheduled, Done, Cancelled). This is dynamically derived from the status of its children, but allows for a manual override for edge cases.\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl1
\f2\fs26 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 X-PROJECT-PRIORITY
\f1\fs24 : An integer used strictly for sorting the order of Projects in the UI.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The Relationship (
\f4\fs26 RELATED-TO
\f0\fs24 ):
\f1\b0  Any Event, Task, or Note that belongs to a Project includes the 
\f2\fs26 RELATED-TO: <Project-UID>
\f1\fs24 . The client builds an in-memory graph on load.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 B. Events (
\f4\fs30\fsmilli15210 VEVENT
\f0\fs28 )\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Core Properties:
\f1\b0  
\f2\fs26 DTSTART
\f1\fs24 , 
\f2\fs26 DTEND
\f1\fs24 , 
\f2\fs26 SUMMARY
\f1\fs24 , 
\f2\fs26 DESCRIPTION
\f1\fs24 , 
\f2\fs26 LOCATION
\f1\fs24 , 
\f2\fs26 RELATED-TO
\f1\fs24  (Optional Project Link).\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Logic:
\f1\b0  Standard rendering. "Duplicate" button replaces complex 
\f2\fs26 RRULE
\f1\fs24  recurring logic.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 C. Tasks (
\f4\fs30\fsmilli15210 VTODO
\f0\fs28 )\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Core Properties:
\f1\b0  
\f2\fs26 SUMMARY
\f1\fs24  (Title), 
\f2\fs26 DUE
\f1\fs24  (Deadline), 
\f2\fs26 STATUS
\f1\fs24  (NEEDS-ACTION, COMPLETED, CANCELLED), 
\f2\fs26 RELATED-TO
\f1\fs24  (Optional Project Link).\
\ls5\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Sub-tasks & Prerequisites (UI-Masked Markdown):
\f1\b0 \
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl1\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Stored entirely within the 
\f2\fs26 DESCRIPTION
\f1\fs24  field as markdown checklists.\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl1
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 UX Flow:
\f1\b0  The user 
\f3\i never
\f1\i0  edits the raw markdown. The UI renders dedicated React inputs. On save, Notocal secretly serializes this data back into the markdown format.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 D. Notes (
\f4\fs30\fsmilli15210 VJOURNAL
\f0\fs28 )\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0
\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Core Properties:
\f1\b0  
\f2\fs26 SUMMARY
\f1\fs24  (Title), 
\f2\fs26 DESCRIPTION
\f1\fs24  (Markdown content), 
\f2\fs26 RELATED-TO
\f1\fs24  (Optional Project Link).\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0
\f3\i \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 (Note: Image attachments are intentionally omitted from this spec to maintain pure-text simplicity. Designed to function similarly to the default Apple Notes app).
\f1\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 E. Deletion & Hierarchy Logic\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0
\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Principle:
\f1\b0  Deletion works hierarchically, not laterally.\
\ls7\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Project Deletion:
\f1\b0  Prompts the user: 
\f3\i "Delete all events, tasks, and notes under this project?"
\f1\i0  (Default: No). If No, the children's 
\f2\fs26 RELATED-TO
\f1\fs24  links are severed, and they effectively drop into a global "No Project" bucket.\
\ls7\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Task Deletion:
\f1\b0  If a task has sub-tasks, the UI prompts for the deletion of the sub-tasks as well.\
\ls7\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Prerequisite Deletion:
\f1\b0  Deleting a prerequisite merely removes the relational link; it does not delete the target task itself.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 4. UI/UX: The Multi-Pane Desktop Layout\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 Top Navigation (Slide-Down Bar)\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls8\ilvl0
\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Behavior:
\f1\b0  Hidden by default. Slides down when the cursor hits the top edge. Includes a "Pin" toggle to lock it as a permanent top bar.\
\ls8\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Main Views & Shortcuts:
\f1\b0  Switchable via number keys.\
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls8\ilvl1
\f2\fs26 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 [1]
\f1\fs24  
\f0\b Projects
\f1\b0 \
\ls8\ilvl1
\f2\fs26 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 [2]
\f1\fs24  
\f0\b Calendar
